# Project Structure

The project is based Domain Driven Development but not limited to it. It also uses Hexagonal and Plugin Architectures.

- Always think hard before implement a fancy design pattern. Ask yourself if we really need and the value that it can add to the users/project. But still, stick to DDD, Hexagonal and Plugin patterns.
- Backend code is in `yubarta`
- Domains are in `yubarta/core`
- Adapters are in `yubarta/drivers`
- Interfaces are in `yubarta/entrypoints`
- `yubarta/common` serves as a place where we put code that is shared across all layers
- `yubarta/controllers` is where we place the application logic
- When I ask to add a new provider, consider use a Plugin Architecture Pattern
- Use dataclasses for domain/model classes
- Use classical mapping of SQLAlchemy when a new domain/model is added 
